      "writtenOn": "2021-01-06T21:56:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It looks like with bi-directional LSRX cables can train the link in uni-direction as well. So even if the tbt cable supports bi-directional link training, we need to set the retimer and mux to uni-direction for operation in USB4 mode.\nThe main comment cites USB4 table 13-7. If the above statement is accurate, then this statement from the table would be inoperative: \"The Sideband Channel ... shall operate as a USB4 Sideband Channel [if] ... The Link is over either a Passive Cable or an Active Cable with unidirectional Re-timers.\"\n\nIf Intel believes that statement to be inoperative, can you confirm explicitly?",
